  "notes": [
    "M6 is credential-free and local. It does not claim a hosted Cloudflare deployment, account, namespace, or production-like preview; that separately authorized external gate begins at M9.",
    "Cloudflare does not expose an exact per-isolate resident-memory counter. The gate records core-managed high-water separately, measures absolute Workerd process RSS, and runs a raw Durable Object SQLite control that reproduces the runtime-owned row-count effect without instantiating filesystem caches.",
    "An unknown Cloudflare account or plan reports the conservative decimal 1,000,000,000-byte database and runtime-owned journal ceiling. Explicit paid-plan configuration is clamped at the documented decimal 10,000,000,000-byte maximum.",
    "The accepted Node predecessor and faithful-local Durable Object selections have separate per-target deadlines. Exact clean-candidate component runs completed in 551,615 ms and 558,425 ms respectively; their sequential aggregate is not a target runtime.",
    "The exact smoke completed 9,056 operations and three runtime evictions in 39,866 ms as part of the exact clean-candidate Durable Object target.",
    "After the measured scale phase, the complete maintenance fault matrix runs in one isolated process lane while the portable, migration, filesystem-fault, and publication-fault selections run serially in a second lane. This scheduling change preserves every fixture and fault position while keeping the faithful-local target below its deadline under observed host variance.",
    "Replication is not part of the M5/M6 scale gate. The unchanged 100,000-row fixture remains mandatory for enumeration, accounting, verification, and collection here; Node-to-Node and Node-to-Durable-Object replication is added at M8."
  ]
